//RS /// expression pipeline, so a command-line expression and the same text typed
//RS /// into `jet repl` cannot disagree — there is no second expression evaluator
//RS /// (I8) and no second set of semantics (I9). This function only marshals the
//RS /// result into D-EVAL1=A's rendering: pretty by default, `--json` for stable
//RS /// machine JSON with program output kept off stdout.
